Real Time Examples of Debouncing and Throttling!!

Debouncing → Wait until input stops, then react.
Think about real life:
• In interviews, we usually wait until the interviewer finishes the question before answering.
• During meetings, we don’t respond after every sentence.
• Doctors let patients explain symptoms before giving suggestions.
• Parents hear the whole story before reacting.
• Customer support waits for the complete issue.
• Friends finish telling the story before hearing your opinion.
• Teachers complete the question before students answer.
• Voice assistants wait for silence before processing.
• Moderators allow one person to finish before moving ahead.
• Negotiations happen after hearing the full offer.

Throttling → Allow continuous input, but control how often you react.
Again, real life examples:
• Managers ask for updates weekly, not every minute.
• Teachers monitor noise periodically.
• News channels provide updates every few minutes.
• Sports commentators don’t narrate every movement.
• Conference hosts announce at intervals.
• Parents check homework progress occasionally.
• Traffic announcements repeat after some time.
• Team leads take scheduled status checks.
• Cricket score updates happen periodically.
• GPS updates location every few seconds.

